# Futuristic/Cyber Widget Style

Use this style when creating or updating Flutter UI in screens and widgets.

- Prefer layered dark surfaces with neon accents:
  - Base backgrounds: near-black or deep blue-gray.
  - Accent colors: cyan, magenta, violet, or electric blue.
- Build depth with subtle glow and edge highlights:
  - Use `BoxShadow` with low opacity and soft blur.
  - Add thin borders to suggest holographic panels.
- Favor sharp, geometric structure:
  - Rounded corners should be small-to-medium, not bubbly.
  - Use clear spacing rhythm and grid-like alignment.
- Emphasize readability and contrast:
  - Keep body text high contrast against dark surfaces.
  - Use accents for interactive or status elements only.
- Animate sparingly and with purpose:
  - Short, smooth transitions (`AnimatedContainer`, `TweenAnimationBuilder`).
  - Avoid distracting continuous effects.
- Build UI as composable, reusable widgets:
  - Extract repeated visual patterns into small widgets (cards, badges, tiles, section headers).
  - Prefer stateless presentational widgets with clear constructor inputs.
  - Reuse style constants/tokens for colors, spacing, radius, and shadow values.
  - Compose screens from these building blocks instead of duplicating inline `Container` trees.

## Example Direction

```dart
class CyberPanel extends StatelessWidget {
  const CyberPanel({super.key, required this.child});

  final Widget child;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Container(
      decoration: BoxDecoration(
        color: const Color(0xFF0B1020),
        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),
        border: Border.all(color: const Color(0xFF39D5FF).withOpacity(0.45)),
        boxShadow: const [BoxShadow(color: Color(0x5539D5FF), blurRadius: 18)],
      ),
      padding: const EdgeInsets.all(12),
      child: child,
    );
  }
}

class StatusBadge extends StatelessWidget {
  const StatusBadge({super.key, required this.label});

  final String label;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return CyberPanel(
      child: Text(label, style: const TextStyle(color: Color(0xFF9FE8FF))),
    );
  }
}

// Compose screens from reusable pieces.
Column(
  children: const [
    StatusBadge(label: 'ONLINE'),
    SizedBox(height: 8),
    StatusBadge(label: 'UNLOCK READY'),
  ],
)
```
